kind: graph
semantic_diff: >-
  Vocabulary rename only, approved by the user. Three keys change name: the
  runtime_bindings block is now write_limits, control_endpoints is now control_nodes,
  and the state field terminal_classification is now final_status. Description text
  now uses the plain words of the approved glossary (round for lap, apply for land,
  revision log for ledger (plan row where ledger meant the living plan's row), write report for census, retry copy for re-cut, stop limit
  for breaker, external for world-produced, and the rest). No node, outcome, edge,
  check, or role is added, removed, or renamed. No meaning changes. Counts unchanged:
  32 nodes, 96 edges, 17 checks, 89 outcomes.
user_only_changes: approved
plan_evidence: verified
usage_evidence: field
changelog_entry: >-
  Revision 10 (graph): plain-English vocabulary. Keys renamed: write_limits (was
  runtime_bindings), control_nodes (was control_endpoints), final_status (was
  terminal_classification). Description text uses the approved glossary. No meaning change.
approval: >-
  User, 2026-09-11: "rename it all in one go, fuck the ledger migration, all you're
  doing is replacing it with words I can understand okay??? I don't know what
  envelope_exceeded means, replace with simple english YAML key" and, on the glossary:
  "these are fine as is: traversal, socratic, semantic diff, semantic_change_required,
  successor, approve all others".
